## Docs screenshots (`docs/scripts/shots/`)

Figures are **light/dark pairs** under `docs/src/assets/<section>/`; replacing one is overwriting the
file. Capture is scripted, Windows-only: `capture.ps1` (dot-sourced: `Set-ClientSize`,
`Save-ClientShot`, `Set-OsTheme`, `Invoke-ClientClick/Scroll`), `shots.json` (per-figure manifest),
`contentbox.mjs` / `controlbox.mjs` (derive callout and control rects from pixels), `audit.mjs`
(six checks), `optimize.mjs` (lossless re-encode). Human docs: `docs/src/content/docs/building.md`.

| Rule | Why |
|------|-----|
| Capture the **client rect in physical pixels**, never a hand-crop | hand-cropping gave six sizes and a 1–2px desktop rim bleeding through the window edge |
| PowerShell must call `SetProcessDPIAware()` first | otherwise a 175% display silently returns logical pixels |
| Canonical size comes from the app's `config.yaml` window size | resize until Operations stops scrolling; `audit.mjs` fails a scrollbar unless `scrolls: true` |
| Flip themes with `Set-OsTheme` **in place**, snapshot + restore | `ui.theme: system` repaints without losing scroll/staged edits/open dialogs |
| Blur `[autofocus]` fields (click the dialog heading) before capturing | a blinking caret lands in one theme's frame only |
| Callout frames: equal left/right clearance, same x per tab (Settings 14, Operations 474), may cross the scrollbar | treating the scrollbar as a boundary once ate the right pad and put the stroke on the row buttons |
| Redaction rects must sit **inside** the control (`controlbox.mjs`) | eyeballed rects overhung the input border by 4–8px |
| The averaging **downscale** destroys the data; the bicubic **upscale** is cosmetic | reverting it to nearest-neighbour buys no safety |
| Run `optimize.mjs` after a re-shoot | `System.Drawing` PNGs are ~14% larger than needed; it asserts pixel-identity |

`audit.mjs` proves a redaction stayed inside its control, **not** that it covers the right thing —
check every redacted figure by eye. Policy lives in `shots.json`'s `redactPolicy`.

## Out of scope (v1)

SSH tunnels, encrypted config vault, audit log file, reading remote `pg_hba.conf`.

## Safety (implemented)

- Production badge + confirm popup (`askConfirm('Production', …)`); frontend sends `confirmProduction: true` after it. No checkbox.
- Remove role: in-app `<dialog id="confirm-dialog">` (not `window.confirm()` — broken in Wails WebView)
- No in-UI credential fields; secrets never written to config

## Pending / follow-ups

1. User may need different function signatures on server — adjust `call` templates and literals only in config (not app code) when possible.
2. Do **not** edit `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` unless user explicitly asks.

## Package dependencies (avoid import cycles)

| Package | May import | Must not import |
|---------|------------|-----------------|
| `internal/model` | (stdlib only) | other `internal/*` |
| `internal/calltemplate` | stdlib | `config`, `pg`, `commands`, `batch` |
| `internal/config` | `model`, `calltemplate` | `pg` |
| `internal/pg` | `model`, `calltemplate`, pgx | `config` |
| `internal/commands` | `model`, `config` | — |
| `internal/update` | `model`, `version`, stdlib | `config`, `pg`, `commands`, `batch` |

- `internal/update` checks GitHub Releases (`CheckForUpdate` binding); opt-in auto-check on startup via `ui.check_for_updates` (default ON, `UISettings.AutoCheck()`); `SetUpdateSeenVersion` suppresses repeat startup popups.
- Config validates templates via `calltemplate.ValidateCallTemplate`, not `pg`.
- **`internal/pg` tests must not import `internal/config`** (creates cycle: config → calltemplate ← pg test → config).
- Cross-package SQL tests: `commands` + `calltemplate`, or `calltemplate` alone.

## Tests & CI

- Run **`make test`** (or `go test ./...`) before committing.
- GitHub Actions: `.github/workflows/test.yml` on push/PR.
- When adding an operation: extend `AllowedPlaceholders`, `commands.BuildArgs`, defaults in `config/store.go`, tests in `calltemplate`, `commands`, `config`.

## Conventions when changing code

- Minimal diffs; match existing package layout and naming.
- JSON struct tags on model types for Wails (camelCase).
- After changing Go bindings, run `wails dev` or `wails build` to refresh `frontend/wailsjs/`.
- Comments only for non-obvious business rules.
